    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on three primary anchors today: **James Wood** (77.49), **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91), and **Mickey Moniak** (75.75). **James Wood** provides our highest ceiling, benefiting from an elite xwOBA of .422 and a favorable matchup against a hittable Ritchie, while **Mickey Moniak**\u2019s projection is bolstered significantly by a +14% dynamic platoon edge and a +14% park factor, making him a high-efficiency play despite facing a veteran arm like Lugo. **Brice Turang** (73.40) remains a must-start; his matchup against Ure\u00f1a is maximized by his role in the leadoff spot and a generous 85% SB success probability against a slow-working starter. **Isaac Paredes** (64.29) rounds out the top tier, as his +9% platoon advantage against Rocker provides the necessary floor to keep him locked into the 3B slot.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved leaving **Seiya Suzuki** (46.96) on the bench. While his talent is clear, the combination of a tough outing against Cole and a detrimental \"Wind In\" factor suppressed his efficiency below that of **Henry Bolte** and **Jose Caballero**. We are monitoring the situation for **Dalton Rushing**, as his status remains \"Lineup Pending.\" Should he drop out or his projected #9 spot shift further down, his value is already precariously close to our floor at 41.30. Caution is also warranted with **Corbin Carroll** (59.15), whose score is heavily depressed by a brutal matchup against the elite stuff of Williams and an \"Elite Catcher\" pop time risk that complicates his stolen base outlook. With **Vinnie Pasquantino** confirmed on the IL, we are leaning heavily on the depth provided by **Josh Naylor** and **Travis Bazzana** to stabilize the middle of the order while we navigate these challenging pitching matchups.",
